  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kanom krok makes 24 pancakes and takes about 35 minutes. Traditional kanom krok use a special dimpled cast-iron pan with 12 or 14 round moulds. A standard frying pan with a lid works as a close substitute, making flat rather than domed pancakes. The outer shell uses "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "glutinous rice",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "glutinous-rice"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " flour, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "jasmine rice",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "jasmine-rice"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " flour, and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "coconut milk",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "coconut-milk"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The filling uses coconut milk and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "caster sugar",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "caster-sugar"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The batter needs rice flour, not plain flour. The two are not interchangeable. Look for ground rice or rice flour in the world food aisle. Use equal parts glutinous rice flour and plain rice flour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 6,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "short-grain-rice",
              "amount": 100,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "ground to flour, or use shop-bought glutinous rice flour",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Shell batter"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "jasmine-rice",
              "amount": 100,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "ground to flour, or use shop-bought rice flour",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Shell batter"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "coconut-milk",
              "amount": 200,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": null,
