              "groupLabel": "Shell batter"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Shell batter"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "coconut-milk",
              "amount": 150,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Filling"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Filling"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "vegetable-oil",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "for greasing",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make the shell batter. Whisk both flours with the 200 ml coconut milk, 1 tablespoon of {{caster-sugar}}, and a pinch of salt until smooth. Set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make the filling. Stir the 150 ml coconut milk with 2 tablespoons of caster sugar and a pinch of salt until dissolved. Set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat a small non-stick frying pan over medium heat. Brush with oil."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour 1 tablespoon of shell batter into each mould space or in small circles in the pan. Cook for 1 minute until the edges look set."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Spoon 1 teaspoon of the filling into the centre of each pancake. Cover the pan with a lid and cook for 2 to 3 minutes until the filling is just set but still wobbly at the centre."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use a thin spatula to lift each pancake. The underside should be golden. Serve immediately. The filling should still be slightly soft and creamy."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Pancakes are sticking to the pan",
              "cause": "Pan not well oiled or not fully preheated",
              "fix": "Oil the pan generously and allow it to come up to temperature before adding the batter."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Filling has run out from the centre",
              "cause": "Shell was not set enough before the filling was added",
              "fix": "Wait until the edges of the shell are clearly set and the centre is no longer liquid before adding the filling."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Batter is lumpy",
              "cause": "Flour and coconut milk not whisked thoroughly",
              "fix": "Whisk well and pass through a fine sieve if there are persistent lumps."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kanom krok are sold from street carts across Thailand, especially in the morning and at weekend markets. The traditional pan is a heavy cast-iron disc with shallow hemispherical moulds that produce perfectly domed pancakes. The skill is in the timing: the outer shell should be crispy at the base while the filling remains soft and molten inside. Street vendors develop this judgement over years. At home, a small non-stick pan with a lid replicates the steaming effect that sets the filling without overcooking the shell."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
